==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Only One Rarity}}

==Battleground==
*7 [[Baa Baa]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[Gabriel]] spawns after 8.67 seconds<sup>260f</sup>.
*3 [[Gory|Gories]] spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*4 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Mr. Puffington]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Boraphim]] spawns as the boss.
**8 [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**1 [[Chickful A]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
**5 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 63.33~66.67 seconds<sup>1,900f~2,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
An anti-climactic finish to a difficult gauntlet of stages, Round 5 is not particularly challenging. At the beginning, you have the option to stall Mr. Puffington until every other enemy has been exhausted. This allows you to deal with Boraphim almost entirely on its own. While not easy, this isn't a particularly difficult task either. However, you're under a fairly strict time limit, as Chickful A and Relic Doges will start spawning after 30 and 50 seconds respectively. The Relic Doges, in particular, are slightly buffed and pose a significant threat by applying curse to your Angel-targeting units. Attack Up combos are recommended to make defeating Boraphim far quicker and more efficient.

Once Boraphim is dead, Chickful A and the Relic Doges no longer pose a significant threat.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
===='''Normal Cats'''====
*[[Superfeline (Normal Cat)|Superfeline II/True Superfeline]]: With Massive Damage against Relic enemies, they can two or three-shot the Relic Doges at higher levels. Their [[Omni Strike]] almost guarantees they never miss an attack, and they can also help chip away at Boraphim.
*[[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|The Flying Cat]]: Deals decent damage and occasionally applies [[Weaken]] to Angels. They can help stall Boraphim when Superfeline is on cooldown.

===='''Special Cats'''====
*[[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N/Idi:NX]]: Can instantly dispose of Mr. Puffington as long as peons are kept in check. She can also finish off Boraphim if your main damage dealers are unable to do so before biting the dust.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Fills a similar role to Idi:N and can act as an additional rusher if Idi is on cooldown. Keep in mind that even at level 50, he can't OHKO the Relic Doges; he works best with Attack Up combos to maximize his effectiveness.
*[[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Catcratres]]: If unlocked, he serves as a main DPS and Crowd Control unit for Boraphim and the Gabriels. His relatively high freeze chance, combined with his Omni Strike and high attack rate, allows him to occasionally perma-stall every Angel enemy on the field. While his damage isn't the highest, his [[Conjure]] ability adds an additional 45k damage on command, while applying Weaken.

===='''Rare Cats'''====
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: Boosting him is highly recommended, as Ramen is one of the few non-Uber meatshields available to stall the Angel enemies in this stage. He performs decently in this role, capable of stalling Boraphim and Gabriels for extended periods. Additional support goes a long way though, as it takes time to redeploy him once he dies. Do whatever you can to keep him alive as long as possible.

===='''Super Rare Cats'''====
*[[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Prof. Cat Jobs]]: His 99% Weaken is immensely useful for stalling Boraphim and occasionally sniping Relic Doges with his Surge attacks. If enemies reach him, his [[Survive]] ability guarantees one reposition opportunity. However, his sluggish speed, and high survivability can occasionally bar you from deploying other Super Rare units when needed. Despite these downsides, he performs exceptionally well in this stage. It should be noted that using other Weaken units will override the 99% Weaken effect, and bring it back down to the usual 50%. If your strategy relies on Cat Jobs, do '''NOT''' use The Flying Cat, or Catcrates' Conjure.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Her high Single Attack damage cripples Boraphim if properly stalled. She can also handle Relic Doges, Gories, and BaaBaas at the beginning for extra cash.

